{"body":"To speed up functuonal tests maybe use less epoches ?","comments":[{"author":"paulzierep","body":"Implemented — functional tests can now run with fewer epochs.\n\n- **Why the tests looked slow:** COMEBin's `train` defaults to `--epochs 200` and `run_comebin.sh` never exposed it, so every invocation inherited the full budget. The two small runs so far (41 s / 43 s) actually died on bugs long before epoch count mattered — but once fixed, a full 200-epoch budget would apply, so the flag is worth adding now.\n\n- **What changed:**\n  - `COMEBin/run_comebin.sh` (branch `comebin-small-fix`): new optional **`-E INT`** → passes `--epochs` to `main.py train`; default stays `200` (upstream behavior, so benchmark comparability is untouched).\n  - `scripts/run_small_test.sh`: new **`EPOCHS`** env var, **default 30**, recorded in `run_meta.txt` as `epochs: …`, and only passed when the CLI supports `-E` (same defensive pattern as the existing `-d`/`-s` checks). `--earlystop` still arms and can stop even earlier.\n\n- **Usage:** `EPOCHS=10 bash scripts/run_small_test.sh runs/small_test 8` — or rely on the new default of 30.\n\nFull benchmark runs (`run_comebin_fix.sh`, baseline rerun) intentionally keep the full 200-epoch budget so results stay comparable to the baseline row.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T04:59:09Z","id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWi6twQ","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/10#issuecomment-5807975873"}],"number":10,"state":"OPEN","title":"Try less epoches","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T04:59:09Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/10"}
