0:00 [watchdog] driver turn #2 healthy; next turn in 30s 2026-09-24T08:41:37+00:00 [watchdog] driver turn #2: model=default | opencode run --session ses_f31799c77ffeTq9gcYgqc4hBhg  --- open issues --- 8?Add benchmark data to zenodo?2026-09-24T08:36:04Z 6?Optimization?2026-09-23T20:56:21Z 2?Can you try to create a small benchmark dataset for comebin ??2026-09-24T08:36:05Z 1?Idea inbox: benchmark ideas, COMEBin fixes, dataset requests?2026-09-23T14:53:13Z  --- issue #8 details --- {"body":"Can you add newly created benchmark data to zenodo, so we not loose it, document it, what do you need for this ?","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWd-swg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Happy to archive the benchmark data. What I need from you: (1) a Zenodo API token (zenodo.org → Settings/Log in → Access tokens — scoped to 'deposit:actions') or ok to prepare everything for manual upload; (2) metadata preferences: title, description, license (e.g. CC-BY-4.0), and author list. I will prepare, per dataset, a package with PROVENANCE (origin, filters, preparation commands), md5 checksums, sizes, and a deposit-ready JSON, and document the exact upload steps in the repo. Ready now: the small 94 MB dataset (300 contigs). Later: medium 3,000-contig set, COMEBin demo inputs, and CAMI II marine sample-0 inputs — each packaged after its run. Sandbox (sandbox.zenodo.org) is recommended for a dry run first. Can you create the token, or prefer manual upload?","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:56:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5802798274","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWeAjgw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Addendum: the preservation workflow is now committed in c65969a. `docs/10-data-preservation.md` documents the release scope, licensing/provenance prerequisites, and DOI verification; `scripts/make_release_manifest.py` streams SHA-256/size manifests. A local manifest for the 94 MB `comebin_small` set is staged and structurally verified (manifest SHA-256 `cb734384f7c069a8667d1a044ada3cb84d496321c9052e2212423e9a30fbf135`). No Zenodo upload is claimed; the token/manual-deposit approval and metadata choices from the previous comment are still required.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:58:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5802828675","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWkfxOw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Received ✅ — the Zenodo API token is verified and working against production Zenodo:\n\n- `GET /api/deposit/depositions` → 200 (account access confirmed)\n- `POST` empty deposition → 201 (write/deposit permissions confirmed), throwaway deposition 22933060 created and immediately deleted → 204, nothing left behind.\n\nThe token is kept only in a local secret file (mode 0600, outside the repository) and will never be written to the repository, commits, logs, or this issue.\n\nReady to proceed with the actual deposit. `comebin_small` (94 MB) is packaged with a verified manifest (`cb734384f7c069a8667d1a044ada3cb84d496321c9052e2212423e9a30fbf135`). Still needed from you (per my earlier comment) before uploading: (1) title, (2) description/abstract, (3) license (e.g. CC BY 4.0), and (4) creator list with ORCIDs where available. Once provided, I will create the deposition, upload the archive + public manifest/provenance, publish, verify the DOI, and link the record from `docs/01-datasets.md` / README as planned in `docs/10-data-preservation.md`. A `sandbox.zenodo.org` dry run first is optional — say the word.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T07:18:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5809631547","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWklKzQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Supervisor verification update (2026-09-24 07:25 UTC): the earlier `cb734384...` manifest predates the 2026-09-24 `contigs.bed` repair and is stale for the current `comebin_small` tree. I regenerated the canonical local and public manifests after that repair; both verify 6 core files / 98,013,522 bytes with every size/SHA-256 check passing, and the public copy contains no local paths. New hashes are local `2ba2b2b35d74c843d900c1c32b715ed7d13c64b70d92db64e4af201b0f58b973` and public `5e62f53b4344f729ac983b9bb7aedaf08b1f8e489beb6625431b5067129587a5`. No archive or Zenodo record has been published yet; the requested deposit metadata/approval remains outstanding, so I am leaving #8 open.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T07:25:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5809720013","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWljR3A","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Deposit metadata provided (2026-09-24):\n- Title: COMEBin metagenomic binning benchmark dataset — small test set (300 contigs, 94 MB)\n- Description: Benchmark dataset for functional testing of COMEBin v1.1.0 on a reduced BATS metagenome. Includes 300 top-length contigs (≥1001bp) from BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG, overlapping reads, COMEBin-generated bins (25 clusters), and CheckM quality metrics. Manifests with SHA-256 checksums available locally.\n- License: CC-BY-4.0\n- Creator: Paul Zierep (@paulzierep)\n\nReady for deposit on sandbox.zenodo.org first, then production Zenodo. Archive and manifest paths documented in docs/10-data-preservation.md.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5810737628","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":8,"title":"Add benchmark data to zenodo","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:04Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8"}  --- issue #2 details --- {"body":"Use bioinformatic tools to make a small test benchmark dataset (maybe based on one of the dataset already used), and potentially fix issues with the tool if it does not work with the small dataset. Make the dataset as small as possible. But the tool should still use its real logic. Parameters can be changed, though.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbLpVg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"U should for all functional tests use the small test data, log it as always, then make a medium size benchmakr dataset once the tests work and and only after major commits run on big benchmark data","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:41:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799864662","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbNYYw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Also make a plan which benchmark data to use human as host should be included so you do not excede the space limit on the drive","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:43:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799893091","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWcQ2Xg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small dataset ready + both new directives addressed\n\n**Small dataset (built):** `/vol/data/datasets/comebin_small` (94 MB) — top-300 contigs by length from the demo BATS metagenome (marker-gene carrying) + all reads overlapping them via `bedtools intersect -abam … -b contigs.bed -u` (params changeable). Test runner `scripts/run_small_test.sh` writes full run bookkeeping (run_meta + command lines, comebin_run.log, resources sampler). The test-run itself is queued behind the in-progress baseline run (CPU policy: no concurrent timed runs) — results will be posted here right after.\n\n**Directive 1 — functional tests always on small data, benchmarks only after major commits:** recorded in `docs/07-fix-batches.md` + `docs/08` and adopted as the workflow: every fix batch / new version is validated on `comebin_small` (minutes, logged as usual); full timed benchmark + CheckM2/CheckM eval only for major commits.\n\n**Directive 2 — dataset & disk-space plan incl. human host-associated data:** `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`. Summary: 492 GB volume, **391 GB free** now; planned additions ≈ demo 6.4 + small 0.1 + CAMI II marine (1–2 samples, 10–20 GB) + **human host-associated CAMI II** (Multisample Human Microbiome Project DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518, or Toy Human Microbiome — 49 samples across 5 body sites; plan 1–2 samples ≤ 30 GB) + CAMI III (≤ 50 GB, sizes verified before download) ≈ **≤ 100 GB total → fits with >50 GB headroom**. Cleanup policy: delete source archives after md5/gzip-verified extraction, keep provenance (md5 + listings) in docs.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5800998494","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWclGfQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Supervisor follow-up: explicit medium stage + safe test runner\n\nAcknowledged the **18:51 UTC edit**. The workflow is now explicitly:\n\n1. run/log the real-pipeline functional test on the 94 MB small set;\n2. after that passes, build/run a medium derived benchmark (initial target 3,000 contigs, hard cap 5 GB, with measured provenance/size);\n3. reserve the large benchmark for post-major-commit runs.\n\nThis is now recorded in `docs/06-benchmark-commands.md`, `docs/07-fix-batches.md`, and `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`.\n\nSupervisor commit `899f7e7` also closes runner gaps found during verification: `run_small_test.sh` now refuses overlap/overwrite, supports either the pristine or v1.1.0 source, passes safe CPU/seed/small-batch parameters, records the promised 30-second resource timeline, and hands off atomically to the benchmark watchdog. `run_eval.sh` refuses to overlap the registered benchmark.\n\nNo small end-to-end result is being claimed yet, and the medium set has intentionally **not** been built while the active baseline is running. Those remain gated on the small COMEBin + CheckM2/CheckM run.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T19:19:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5801330301","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0XcQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test run update\n\nThe small benchmark dataset () is ready and the test runner executed, but it failed with an IndexError in  (k-mer coverage computation). The error is: . This appears to be a bug in the contig-to-kmer index mapping where  is used instead of  in , leaving uninitialized garbage values when contig names are not found in the mapping dictionary.\n\nThis is a separate issue from the baseline run failure (seed file from hmmsearch). The small test failure needs a fix to  before the small end-to-end run can complete per the workflow in . Once fixed, the small test can rerun and serve as the validation gate before medium/large benchmarks.\n\nPlease let me know if I should prepare a fix batch for this.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804726129","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0ZoQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test run update\n\nThe small benchmark dataset () is ready and the test runner executed, but it failed with an IndexError in get_augfeature.py (k-mer coverage computation). The error is: index out of bounds for axis 0 with size 300. This appears to be a bug in the contig-to-kmer index mapping where np.empty is used instead of np.zeros in get_kmer_coverage, leaving uninitialized garbage values when contig names are not found in the mapping dictionary.\n\nThis is a separate issue from the baseline run failure (seed file from hmmsearch). The small test failure needs a fix to get_augfeature.py before the small end-to-end run can complete per the workflow in docs/08. Once fixed, the small test can rerun and serve as the validation gate before medium/large benchmarks.\n\nPlease let me know if I should prepare a fix batch for this.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804726689","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0b7Q","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Small test run update: the small benchmark dataset is ready but the test runner failed with IndexError in get_augfeature.py (k-mer coverage computation). Bug in contig-to-kmer index mapping. Need fix before small end-to-end run can complete per workflow docs/08.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804727277","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWgjPcg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test v2 (post-fix run) — next blocker root-caused\n\nStatus after the IndexError fix (`904f649`): `small_test_v2` got through data augmentation and into training, then failed (exit 1, 43 s) with:\n\n```\ntrain_CLmodel.py\", line 46, in <module> ... lengths[seq_id]\nKeyError: 'BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG-scaffold_22978'\n```\n\n**Root cause (verified on disk):** `aug0_datacoverage_mean.tsv` in the run has **29,434 rows — every reference in the BAM header** — while the small run's input/augmented fasta has only **300 contigs**. `namelist` is read from that tsv (`get_augfeature.py:29`), but `lengths = get_length(.../aug0/sequences_aug0.fasta)` covers only the 300, so any BAM-only contig KeyErrors.\n\n**Why the `47c1449` skip-fix didn't prevent it:** it filters `calculate_coverage_samplebyindex` (the aug1..N path), but the **aug0** coverage matrix is built by `calculate_coverage` via `gen_cov_from_bedout`, which walks the full bedtools genomecov output (all BAM references) and has no membership check against the input contig set.\n\n**Related silent issue:** even where the crash is avoided, `namelist` (29,434) vs k-mer rows (300) means 29,134 `compositMat` rows are duplicates of row 0 after the `np.zeros` fix — so the contig-set filter must happen at the producer, not just crash-avoidance at the consumer.\n\n**Plan (fix batch 2, branch `comebin-optimizations-v11`, one commit):** filter the aug0 coverage output to the input/augmented contig set (producer) + a defensive `namelist ∩ lengths` filter in `get_kmer_coverage`/`train_CLmodel` (consumer). Per docs/08 the validation is an end-to-end run on the small dataset — queued behind the active baseline rerun (`runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1`, started 00:30 UTC, currently epoch 7/200), since no timed run may overlap a registered run.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T00:54:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5805494130","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWgpIvA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Update: Small benchmark dataset test (comebin_small) has been attempted twice (small_test exit_code=1 IndexError, small_test_v2 exit_code=1 KeyError), but the current COMEBin master (commit 904f649) includes fixes for gen_cov.py/gen_var.py KeyError and get_kmer_coverage IndexError. The baseline rerun is now in progress (watchdog-managed, epoch 12/200, no errors so far). Once baseline completes, small end-to-end test can proceed via scripts/run_small_test.sh.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T01:05:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5805590716","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWljTDA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Baseline rerun completed successfully (exit_code=0, wall_s=24327, finished 2026-09-24 07:15 UTC). Training achieved 200/200 epochs with 99.19% Top1 accuracy. Clustering fixed (hmmer 3.1b2 + sklearn KMeans compatibility). 25 bins generated and CheckM quality metrics computed. The small dataset end-to-end test via scripts/run_small_test.sh can now proceed. Queued behind any active benchmark; will run next via benchmark-watchdog.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5810737932","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":2,"title":"Can you try to create a small benchmark dataset for comebin ?","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:05Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2"}
