COMEBin metagenomic binning benchmark — small test set
=========================================================

Release scope
-------------
This release contains a reproducible 300-contig derivative of the official
COMEBin BATS demo data, the aligned-read subset used by COMEBin, and the
verified small functional-gate result subset (run small_test_v4). It does not
include raw source archives, CheckM databases, model checkpoints, or bulky
augmentation intermediates.

Origin and selection
--------------------
Source assembly: COMEBin demo file
BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG.scaffolds.min500.fasta.f1k.fasta
Source reads: SRR5720343.bam from the COMEBin demo dataset
Selection: 300 longest contigs from the >=1 kb demo assembly
Read extraction: indexed samtools view -L over an explicit BED interval file
Assembly size: 3,651,343 bp; aligned BAM: 94,078,937 bytes; BAM index included

Functional result
-----------------
COMEBin source branch: comebin-small-fix
COMEBin commit: c8f22e4935a66a0fd58b794489a9021671b15437
Functional run: small_test_v4; 30 epochs; seed 42; 8 threads; 122 s
Output: 3 non-empty bins
CheckM2: mean completeness 26.07%, mean contamination 2.02%
CheckM v1: mean completeness 29.08%, mean contamination 0.71%
The result files are a selected evidence subset; raw augmentation files remain
on the benchmark host and are intentionally excluded from the deposit.

Reproduction outline
--------------------
1. Select the top 300 assembly records by length and emit explicit BED spans.
2. Extract overlapping reads with indexed samtools view -L and index the BAM.
3. Run COMEBin with -n 6, -t 8, -b 256, -e 512, -c 512, -E 30, seed 42.
4. Evaluate the emitted bins with CheckM2 and the CheckM v1 lineage workflow.
5. Verify every file against the public manifest before use.

Licensing
---------
Data are released under CC BY 4.0. COMEBin and third-party tools retain their
 respective licenses; consult the linked upstream projects before redistribution
of software or databases.
EOF
