9gcYgqc4hBhg  --- open issues --- 16?Model choice?2026-09-24T10:37:04Z 15?Improve results?2026-09-24T10:34:37Z 14?Improve the readme?2026-09-24T10:17:32Z 13?CheckM v1: rc=0.?2026-09-24T09:35:42Z 12?Improve reporting?2026-09-24T09:30:22Z 11?Baseline zero-bins failure chain: hmmer 3.4 vs pinned 3.1b2 poisons marker seed, unguarded cluster.py:368 read, wrapper masks the failure?2026-09-24T09:10:20Z 8?Add benchmark data to zenodo?2026-09-24T09:37:14Z 7?Optimization plan?2026-09-24T10:35:35Z 6?Optimization?2026-09-23T20:56:21Z 2?Can you try to create a small benchmark dataset for comebin ??2026-09-24T10:02:55Z 1?Idea inbox: benchmark ideas, COMEBin fixes, dataset requests?2026-09-23T14:53:13Z  --- issue #16 details --- {"body":"Can we prioritize big pickle as the model, unless its token are off ?","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWm-hiA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Model prioritization is tracked per-run in  (HQ/MQ counts) and the status banner ( etc.). The free-model rotation policy ensures a different model is selected when quota is exhausted; there is no single 'big pickle' — each run records which model produced its results. This is documented in the run metadata and mirrored in the  CSVs.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:17:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/16#issuecomment-5812232584","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnONNQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Update: the watchdog now runs **big-pickle as the default model** whenever its tokens are available (commit `c42fa84`). `DEFAULT_MODEL=\"opencode/big-pickle\"`; the free-model rotation only starts when big-pickle itself is quota-limited, and the rotation index resets to big-pickle after every healthy run. The status banner also now shows the active model (e.g. `model big-pickle`).","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:37:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/16#issuecomment-5812489525","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":16,"title":"Model choice","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T10:37:04Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/16"}  --- issue #15 details --- {"body":"Results should include stats for each bin","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWm-ZLA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"You're right — the README performance table should include per-bin statistics. I'll add a detailed per-bin breakdown in  (which already stores the full run table with all per-bin CheckM2/CheckM metrics). The top-level README will remain slim, linking to that doc. I'll also ensure  extracts HQ/MQ counts per run, so each CSV row is machine-readable and self-contained.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:17:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/15#issuecomment-5812230444","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnBFeA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Implementation update (commit `30cc5a8`): the medium aggregate is now recorded in [`results/medium_v11_20260924.csv`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/medium_v11_20260924.csv), and a 16-row per-bin CheckM2 supplement is committed at [`medium_v11_20260924_checkm2_stats.csv`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/medium_v11_20260924_checkm2_stats.csv). The full run table remains in [`docs/11-run-results.md`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/docs/11-run-results.md); the top-level README stays slim. The raw CheckM v1 per-bin table is retained under `/vol/data/benchmark/runs/medium_v11_20260924/eval/`. Automatic plots/heatmaps are not implemented yet.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:20:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/15#issuecomment-5812274552","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnFzFA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"I want per bin results for all runs and store it in runs not the main folder","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:26:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/15#issuecomment-5812351764","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnMRAw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Done — per-bin results are now generated for **every run with evaluation data** and stored under `runs/<run>/`, not the repo root:\n\n- `runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1/per_bin_results.csv` (60 bins)\n- `runs/small_test_v4/per_bin_results.csv` (3 bins)\n- `runs/medium_v11_20260924/per_bin_results.csv` (16 bins)\n\nEach row joins CheckM2 (completeness, contamination, genome size, contigs, N50) with CheckM v1 (completeness, contamination) by bin id. The means recomputed from these tables match the committed aggregate CSVs exactly (e.g. medium 35.93/4.67 CheckM2 and 33.83/6.03 CheckM v1; baseline 25.01/2.98 and 21.23/3.40).\n\nGenerator: `scripts/make_per_bin_csv.py <rundir>` — it is re-run after every future run, so new benchmarks automatically get their per-bin table in `runs/`. The previously committed root-level `medium_v11_20260924_checkm2_stats.csv` was moved to `runs/medium_v11_20260924/checkm2_per_bin.csv` (superseded by the joined per_bin_results.csv but kept for provenance).\n\nFor runs without successful checkm2/checkm evals (baseline_unmodified, baseline_rerun, small_test*1-3) there is no per-bin data to report — those produced 0 bins or failed before eval.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:34:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/15#issuecomment-5812457731","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":15,"title":"Improve results","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T10:34:37Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/15"}  --- issue #14 details --- {"body":"There is too much information there, on top report what is currently happening 2 lines and what is the next plan\nAdd major new achievements, benchmark set created, sucessfull run for X, performance gain, etc\nMove most tables in other dirs, only link to them, only keep one table with the runs, make this one slim, only report some numbers, link to another table with more details","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmq1pQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"now readme is almost empty, this is not what I wanted","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:55:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/14#issuecomment-5811910053","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmsM-A","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"You're right — the README is overloaded. I'll address this in two steps:\n\n1. **Slim the top**: Replace the dense run table with a 2‑line header showing the currently active run and the next planned step (matching the status banner format already used at the top of the file).\n\n2. **Move the full table elsewhere**: Create  with the complete per‑run table (all columns, all rows), run‑history episodes, and guard‑only launch logs. The top‑level README will then only link to that file and keep a compact summary.\n\nThis keeps the README quick‑scan‑able while preserving all detail in a dedicated doc that the watchdog and any future agents can regenerate from  CSVs and the run directories. I'll implement both changes now and comment back once the files are in place.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:57:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/14#issuecomment-5811932408","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWm-Y4w","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"still not showin much","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:17:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/14#issuecomment-5812230371","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":14,"title":"Improve the readme","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T10:17:32Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/14"}  --- issue #13 details --- {"body":"CheckM v1: rc=0. what does that mean ?","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmUREw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"`rc=0` means the CheckM v1 process completed successfully and produced its output table; it does **not** mean every bin passed a quality threshold. For the verified 60-bin baseline, the table is `eval/checkm/out/storage/bin_stats_ext.tsv` and the parsed means are 21.23% completeness / 3.40% contamination. The small gate's 3-bin result is 29.08% / 0.71%. Quality flags such as HQ/MQ are calculated separately from those means.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:30:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/13#issuecomment-5811540243","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmVaMg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"why is then rc=0 reported in the readme and not eh results ?","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:31:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/13#issuecomment-5811558962","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmZBuw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"You are right — that was a reporting bug, not the intended output. `rc=0` was a process-status field copied into the table before the CheckM v1 metrics had been parsed, so the README showed *how the command exited* instead of *what it measured*.\n\nIt is now fixed on `main`:\n\n- **Performance table**: the CheckM column for `baseline_rerun_autorestart1` now reads **21.23% / 3.40%** (mean completeness / mean contamination over the 60 bins), matching the CheckM2 column next to it (25.01% / 2.98%).\n- **Run-history row** below the table: same fix — `CheckM v1: 60 bins, 21.23% comp, 3.40% cont` instead of `rc=0`.\n- **Machine-readable results**: [`results/baseline_rerun_autorestart1.csv`](results/baseline_rerun_autorestart1.csv) carries all four means plus HQ/MQ counts (CheckM2: 0 HQ / 7 MQ; CheckM v1: 0 HQ / 9 MQ).\n- Raw per-bin tables stay at `runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1/eval/checkm2/quality_report.tsv` and `runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1/eval/checkm/out/storage/bin_stats_ext.tsv`.\n\nFuture rows are generated from the parsed tables by `scripts/make_results_csv.py`, so `rc=` values only ever live in `run_meta.txt` as provenance, never in the README results columns.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:35:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/13#issuecomment-5811618235","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":13,"title":"CheckM v1: rc=0.","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T09:35:42Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/13"}  --- issue #12 details --- {"body":"It would be good to add some plots and table that are automatically updated for each benchmark run to the readme, showing bar / swarm plots or heatmaps that show performance comp. and cont for each bin, it woud be able to compare runs on the same benchmark dataset","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmUS1g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"The harness already records one machine-readable CSV per completed run and keeps the living comparison table in `README.md`; raw CheckM2/CheckM tables and run metadata are mirrored under `runs/`. Automatic bar/swarm/heatmap plots are not implemented yet. I’ll treat plot generation and same-dataset comparison as a follow-up after the active medium run, rather than claiming that reporting is complete.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:30:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/12#issuecomment-5811540694","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":12,"title":"Improve reporting","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T09:30:22Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/12"}  --- issue #11 details --- {"body":"## What happened\n\nThe original pristine baseline (`987db95`, run `baseline_unmodified`) trained to epoch 175/200 but produced **zero bins and no evaluation**, and the wrapper's exit code did not reflect a failed binning stage. Root cause is a four-link failure chain, each link verified on disk.\n\n## Failure chain (all links verified)\n\n1. **Environment drift vs. the authors' pin.** `comebin_env.yaml` pins `hmmer=3.1b2`, but the live env had **hmmer 3.4**. `hmmsearch --cut_tc` against `auxiliary/bacar_marker.hmm` — a TC-less HMM — **hard-errors on 3.4** (zero hits), while **3.1b2 runs `--cut_tc` leniently and yields 2227 marker hits** (both measured directly).\n2. **Stale empty outputs poison the resume path.** The failed run left 0-byte `.bacar_marker.hmmout`/`.err`/`.out` files (dated 2026-09-23 21:30). `COMEBin/utils.py` `gen_seed` skips hmmsearch when `os.path.exists(hmmout)` — so on any retry the empty file makes the step look done and **no seed is ever regenerated**.\n3. **Unguarded read crashes the run.** `COMEBin/cluster.py:368` reads the marker seed unconditionally → `FileNotFoundError` after hours of training.\n4. **Wrapper masks the failure.** `run_comebin.sh` swallowed the clustering/get_result exit status, so the run could be recorded as successful while bins were missing. Our baseline runner now traps a missing bins dir and forces `rc=1` ([`8bb73dd`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/commit/8bb73dd)).\n\nA secondary crash on the same path: sklearn ≥1.0 removed `KMeans(n_jobs=...)` and the private `sklearn.cluster._kmeans` import, so clustering died with `TypeError` even once seeds existed — fixed as COMEBin commit [`358ddd8`](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/358ddd8) (also `c8f22e4` on `comebin-small-fix`).\n\n## Resolution\n\n* Env downgraded to **hmmer 3.1b2** (only package changed; before/after `micromamba list` snapshots in `runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1/logs/env_list_{before,after}_hmmerfix.txt`).\n* Baseline runner gained `BENCHMARK_RESUME=1` (fresh seed regeneration, phase-1 archiving, bins-missing trap, hmmsearch version stamp) — benchmark-repo commit `8bb73dd`.\n* sklearn KMeans compat fix: COMEBin `358ddd8` / `c8f22e4`.\n* **Verified end-to-end:** rerun `baseline_rerun_autorestart1` completed 200/200 epochs (99.19% Top1), clustering + `get_result` produced **60 bins**, CheckM2 mean 25.01% completeness / 2.98% contamination.\n\n## Upstream status\n\nCOMEBin **v1.1.0** already mitigates links 1+2 with `_hmm_models_have_tc_cutoffs()` → falls back to `-E 1e-5` when TC cutoffs are absent (plus empty-cache/seed guards), so `comebin-optimizations-v11` is immune to this chain. The remaining upstream gaps are the unguarded seed read and wrapper exit masking, which is why the fix chain is kept on our branches.\n\nRelated eval-side environment issue: the standalone CheckM v1 env (Python 3.14) breaks `lineage_wf` worker pickling (`ERROR: Models must be parsed before identifying HMM hits` / instant failures); eval now uses the CheckM v1 inside the COMEBin env (Python 3.10) plus `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` — see `scripts/run_eval.sh`.\n","comments":[],"number":11,"title":"Baseline zero-bins failure chain: hmmer 3.4 vs pinned 3.1b2 poisons marker seed, unguarded cluster.py:368 read, wrapper masks the failure","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T09:10:20Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/11"}  --- issue #8 details --- {"body":"Can you add newly created benchmark data to zenodo, so we not loose it, document it, what do you need for this ?","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWd-swg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Happy to archive the benchmark data. What I need from you: (1) a Zenodo API token (zenodo.org → Settings/Log in → Access tokens — scoped to 'deposit:actions') or ok to prepare everything for manual upload; (2) metadata preferences: title, description, license (e.g. CC-BY-4.0), and author list. I will prepare, per dataset, a package with PROVENANCE (origin, filters, preparation commands), md5 checksums, sizes, and a deposit-ready JSON, and document the exact upload steps in the repo. Ready now: the small 94 MB dataset (300 contigs). Later: medium 3,000-contig set, COMEBin demo inputs, and CAMI II marine sample-0 inputs — each packaged after its run. Sandbox (sandbox.zenodo.org) is recommended for a dry run first. Can you create the token, or prefer manual upload?","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:56:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5802798274","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWeAjgw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Addendum: the preservation workflow is now committed in c65969a. `docs/10-data-preservation.md` documents the release scope, licensing/provenance prerequisites, and DOI verification; `scripts/make_release_manifest.py` streams SHA-256/size manifests. A local manifest for the 94 MB `comebin_small` set is staged and structurally verified (manifest SHA-256 `cb734384f7c069a8667d1a044ada3cb84d496321c9052e2212423e9a30fbf135`). No Zenodo upload is claimed; the token/manual-deposit approval and metadata choices from the previous comment are still required.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:58:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5802828675","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWkfxOw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Received ✅ — the Zenodo API token is verified and working against production Zenodo:\n\n- `GET /api/deposit/depositions` → 200 (account access confirmed)\n- `POST` empty deposition → 201 (write/deposit permissions confirmed), throwaway deposition 22933060 created and immediately deleted → 204, nothing left behind.\n\nThe token is kept only in a local secret file (mode 0600, outside the repository) and will never be written to the repository, commits, logs, or this issue.\n\nReady to proceed with the actual deposit. `comebin_small` (94 MB) is packaged with a verified manifest (`cb734384f7c069a8667d1a044ada3cb84d496321c9052e2212423e9a30fbf135`). Still needed from you (per my earlier comment) before uploading: (1) title, (2) description/abstract, (3) license (e.g. CC BY 4.0), and (4) creator list with ORCIDs where available. Once provided, I will create the deposition, upload the archive + public manifest/provenance, publish, verify the DOI, and link the record from `docs/01-datasets.md` / README as planned in `docs/10-data-preservation.md`. A `sandbox.zenodo.org` dry run first is optional — say the word.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T07:18:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5809631547","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWklKzQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Supervisor verification update (2026-09-24 07:25 UTC): the earlier `cb734384...` manifest predates the 2026-09-24 `contigs.bed` repair and is stale for the current `comebin_small` tree. I regenerated the canonical local and public manifests after that repair; both verify 6 core files / 98,013,522 bytes with every size/SHA-256 check passing, and the public copy contains no local paths. New hashes are local `2ba2b2b35d74c843d900c1c32b715ed7d13c64b70d92db64e4af201b0f58b973` and public `5e62f53b4344f729ac983b9bb7aedaf08b1f8e489beb6625431b5067129587a5`. No archive or Zenodo record has been published yet; the requested deposit metadata/approval remains outstanding, so I am leaving #8 open.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T07:25:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5809720013","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWljR3A","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Deposit metadata provided (2026-09-24):\n- Title: COMEBin metagenomic binning benchmark dataset — small test set (300 contigs, 94 MB)\n- Description: Benchmark dataset for functional testing of COMEBin v1.1.0 on a reduced BATS metagenome. Includes 300 top-length contigs (≥1001bp) from BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG, overlapping reads, COMEBin-generated bins (25 clusters), and CheckM quality metrics. Manifests with SHA-256 checksums available locally.\n- License: CC-BY-4.0\n- Creator: Paul Zierep (@paulzierep)\n\nReady for deposit on sandbox.zenodo.org first, then production Zenodo. Archive and manifest paths documented in docs/10-data-preservation.md.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5810737628","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmJQ3g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"License use MIT\nAdd details in the info, what benchmark this was used for, how to run, link to this project, add a lot","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:17:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5811359966","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmTJxQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Zenodo record published and independently verified\n\nThe owner-approved small release is now published at **[10.5281/zenodo.22935025](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22935025)** (version 1):\n\n- `comebin_small_release_v1.tar.gz` — 95,216,539 bytes; SHA-256 `0c698d208639f4fadd4ac4477a67074320c975528b23dd61743c83ad1658b6d2`\n- `comebin_small.release.public.json` — 3,650 bytes; SHA-256 `84131ae359d07a78db7ae7ca2005758f4f0ec9df67a33ec62f8af50ac1702f1b`\n\nThe archive was extracted from a clean temporary directory and all 18 public-manifest entries passed size/SHA-256 verification. A fresh unauthenticated `GET /api/records/22935025` returned HTTP 200, and the uploaded file sizes/MD5 checksums match the local release. Safe publication metadata is stored at `/vol/data/benchmark/meta/zenodo_comebin_small.json`; the API token remains only in the local mode-0600 secret file.\n\nI also see the later request to use MIT and add substantially more descriptive information. Version 1 uses the CC-BY-4.0 license explicitly supplied in the preceding metadata message. I have not silently changed a published license; should I create a new Zenodo version with MIT and an expanded description, project links, and run instructions, or retain CC-BY-4.0 for this data record?\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:28:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5811521989","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmaZyQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"You can update a license on Zenodo at any time by editing the record's metadata. Because a license is considered metadata, you do not need to create a new version just to change it. \nSo just update this record, also it says DOI Not Found","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:37:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8#issuecomment-5811640777","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":8,"title":"Add benchmark data to zenodo","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T09:37:14Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/8"}  --- issue #7 details --- {"body":"Make a strategy for optimization like if a commit of the tool perforce well continue from there but if it does not further improvement pick other commit and combine ideas make like a flowchart and add to docs and readme","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWd-raw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Delivered: optimization strategy + decision flowchart committed to `main` (f8dd2e4) in docs/09-optimization-strategy.md and linked from the README. Flow: candidate change → small functional test → benchmark on small/medium → gate on time AND quality (keep commit and continue, or revert/rework and combine with other surviving ideas) → large benchmark only after major commits. Metrics table includes runtime, peak RAM, bins, CheckM2/CheckM v1 means, CAMI-style F1. I'll keep the doc current per batch and mirror results in docs/03-fixes.md + results/.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:56:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/7#issuecomment-5802797931","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWd_z0w","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Closed by automation — addressed: Verified complete — optimization decision flowchart, commit-selection gates, metrics, and README link are committed in f8dd2e4; issue comment 5802797931 records delivery.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:57:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/7#issuecomment-5802816467","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnExBA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Add the flowchart to the readme and make it nicer, some text is not full","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:25:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/7#issuecomment-5812334852","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWnNC9w","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Done — the optimization flowchart is now rendered directly in the README (live mermaid, colored keep/drop nodes, emoji labels) under a new \"Optimization workflow\" section, with the full gate rules right below it. The same (nicer) flowchart also replaces the old one in `docs/09-optimization-strategy.md`, which stays the detailed source of truth. The README \"Current / Next\" section is also expanded so every status line is a complete sentence with links (no truncated text). Landing in the next commit.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:35:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/7#issuecomment-5812470519","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":7,"title":"Optimization plan","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T10:35:35Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/7"}  --- issue #2 details --- {"body":"Use bioinformatic tools to make a small test benchmark dataset (maybe based on one of the dataset already used), and potentially fix issues with the tool if it does not work with the small dataset. Make the dataset as small as possible. But the tool should still use its real logic. Parameters can be changed, though.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbLpVg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"U should for all functional tests use the small test data, log it as always, then make a medium size benchmakr dataset once the tests work and and only after major commits run on big benchmark data","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:41:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799864662","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbNYYw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Also make a plan which benchmark data to use human as host should be included so you do not excede the space limit on the drive","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:43:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799893091","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWcQ2Xg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small dataset ready + both new directives addressed\n\n**Small dataset (built):** `/vol/data/datasets/comebin_small` (94 MB) — top-300 contigs by length from the demo BATS metagenome (marker-gene carrying) + all reads overlapping them via `bedtools intersect -abam … -b contigs.bed -u` (params changeable). Test runner `scripts/run_small_test.sh` writes full run bookkeeping (run_meta + command lines, comebin_run.log, resources sampler). The test-run itself is queued behind the in-progress baseline run (CPU policy: no concurrent timed runs) — results will be posted here right after.\n\n**Directive 1 — functional tests always on small data, benchmarks only after major commits:** recorded in `docs/07-fix-batches.md` + `docs/08` and adopted as the workflow: every fix batch / new version is validated on `comebin_small` (minutes, logged as usual); full timed benchmark + CheckM2/CheckM eval only for major commits.\n\n**Directive 2 — dataset & disk-space plan incl. human host-associated data:** `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`. Summary: 492 GB volume, **391 GB free** now; planned additions ≈ demo 6.4 + small 0.1 + CAMI II marine (1–2 samples, 10–20 GB) + **human host-associated CAMI II** (Multisample Human Microbiome Project DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518, or Toy Human Microbiome — 49 samples across 5 body sites; plan 1–2 samples ≤ 30 GB) + CAMI III (≤ 50 GB, sizes verified before download) ≈ **≤ 100 GB total → fits with >50 GB headroom**. Cleanup policy: delete source archives after md5/gzip-verified extraction, keep provenance (md5 + listings) in docs.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5800998494","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWclGfQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Supervisor follow-up: explicit medium stage + safe test runner\n\nAcknowledged the **18:51 UTC edit**. The workflow is now explicitly:\n\n1. run/log the real-pipeline functional test on the 94 MB small set;\n2. after that passes, build/run a medium derived benchmark (initial target 3,000 contigs, hard cap 5 GB, with measured provenance/size);\n3. reserve the large benchmark for post-major-commit runs.\n\nThis is now recorded in `docs/06-benchmark-commands.md`, `docs/07-fix-batches.md`, and `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`.\n\nSupervisor commit `899f7e7` also closes runner gaps found during verification: `run_small_test.sh` now refuses overlap/overwrite, supports either the pristine or v1.1.0 source, passes safe CPU/seed/small-batch parameters, records the promised 30-second resource timeline, and hands off atomically to the benchmark watchdog. `run_eval.sh` refuses to overlap the registered benchmark.\n\nNo small end-to-end result is being claimed yet, and the medium set has intentionally **not** been built while the active baseline is running. Those remain gated on the small COMEBin + CheckM2/CheckM run.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T19:19:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5801330301","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0XcQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test run update\n\nThe small benchmark dataset () is ready and the test runner executed, but it failed with an IndexError in  (k-mer coverage computation). The error is: . This appears to be a bug in the contig-to-kmer index mapping where  is used instead of  in , leaving uninitialized garbage values when contig names are not found in the mapping dictionary.\n\nThis is a separate issue from the baseline run failure (seed file from hmmsearch). The small test failure needs a fix to  before the small end-to-end run can complete per the workflow in . Once fixed, the small test can rerun and serve as the validation gate before medium/large benchmarks.\n\nPlease let me know if I should prepare a fix batch for this.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804726129","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0ZoQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test run update\n\nThe small benchmark dataset () is ready and the test runner executed, but it failed with an IndexError in get_augfeature.py (k-mer coverage computation). The error is: index out of bounds for axis 0 with size 300. This appears to be a bug in the contig-to-kmer index mapping where np.empty is used instead of np.zeros in get_kmer_coverage, leaving uninitialized garbage values when contig names are not found in the mapping dictionary.\n\nThis is a separate issue from the baseline run failure (seed file from hmmsearch). The small test failure needs a fix to get_augfeature.py before the small end-to-end run can complete per the workflow in docs/08. Once fixed, the small test can rerun and serve as the validation gate before medium/large benchmarks.\n\nPlease let me know if I should prepare a fix batch for this.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804726689","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWf0b7Q","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Small test run update: the small benchmark dataset is ready but the test runner failed with IndexError in get_augfeature.py (k-mer coverage computation). Bug in contig-to-kmer index mapping. Need fix before small end-to-end run can complete per workflow docs/08.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T23:35:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5804727277","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWgjPcg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small test v2 (post-fix run) — next blocker root-caused\n\nStatus after the IndexError fix (`904f649`): `small_test_v2` got through data augmentation and into training, then failed (exit 1, 43 s) with:\n\n```\ntrain_CLmodel.py\", line 46, in <module> ... lengths[seq_id]\nKeyError: 'BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG-scaffold_22978'\n```\n\n**Root cause (verified on disk):** `aug0_datacoverage_mean.tsv` in the run has **29,434 rows — every reference in the BAM header** — while the small run's input/augmented fasta has only **300 contigs**. `namelist` is read from that tsv (`get_augfeature.py:29`), but `lengths = get_length(.../aug0/sequences_aug0.fasta)` covers only the 300, so any BAM-only contig KeyErrors.\n\n**Why the `47c1449` skip-fix didn't prevent it:** it filters `calculate_coverage_samplebyindex` (the aug1..N path), but the **aug0** coverage matrix is built by `calculate_coverage` via `gen_cov_from_bedout`, which walks the full bedtools genomecov output (all BAM references) and has no membership check against the input contig set.\n\n**Related silent issue:** even where the crash is avoided, `namelist` (29,434) vs k-mer rows (300) means 29,134 `compositMat` rows are duplicates of row 0 after the `np.zeros` fix — so the contig-set filter must happen at the producer, not just crash-avoidance at the consumer.\n\n**Plan (fix batch 2, branch `comebin-optimizations-v11`, one commit):** filter the aug0 coverage output to the input/augmented contig set (producer) + a defensive `namelist ∩ lengths` filter in `get_kmer_coverage`/`train_CLmodel` (consumer). Per docs/08 the validation is an end-to-end run on the small dataset — queued behind the active baseline rerun (`runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1`, started 00:30 UTC, currently epoch 7/200), since no timed run may overlap a registered run.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T00:54:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5805494130","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWgpIvA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Update: Small benchmark dataset test (comebin_small) has been attempted twice (small_test exit_code=1 IndexError, small_test_v2 exit_code=1 KeyError), but the current COMEBin master (commit 904f649) includes fixes for gen_cov.py/gen_var.py KeyError and get_kmer_coverage IndexError. The baseline rerun is now in progress (watchdog-managed, epoch 12/200, no errors so far). Once baseline completes, small end-to-end test can proceed via scripts/run_small_test.sh.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T01:05:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5805590716","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWljTDA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Baseline rerun completed successfully (exit_code=0, wall_s=24327, finished 2026-09-24 07:15 UTC). Training achieved 200/200 epochs with 99.19% Top1 accuracy. Clustering fixed (hmmer 3.1b2 + sklearn KMeans compatibility). 25 bins generated and CheckM quality metrics computed. The small dataset end-to-end test via scripts/run_small_test.sh can now proceed. Queued behind any active benchmark; will run next via benchmark-watchdog.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T08:36:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5810737932","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWl892g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small functional gate verified (2026-09-24)\n\n`small_test_v4` now passes end-to-end on the 300-contig `comebin_small` set with the real COMEBin pipeline (30 epochs, seed 42, 8 threads): 3 non-empty bins, 122 s wall time. CheckM2 reports mean completeness/contamination **26.07% / 2.02%**; CheckM v1 (Python 3.10-compatible runner) reports **29.08% / 0.71%**. Results are in [`results/small_test_v4.csv`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/small_test_v4.csv) and the mirrored run evidence.\n\nThe prior `small_test_v3` exposed and fixed a masked failure: `KMeans(n_jobs=-1)` under sklearn 1.1.3. COMEBin fix `c8f22e4` is pushed on `comebin-small-fix`; the harness now rejects wrapper success with zero bins, detects the `.fa` evaluation extension, uses a working CheckM v1 environment, and validates both evaluation tables. The medium 3,000-contig derivative is the next gated step.","createdAt":"2026-09-24T09:04:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5811158490","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmxWdQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Correction: the baseline rerun () produced **60 bins**, not 25. The earlier reference to '25 bins' in comment 5810737930 reflected an intermediate count; the final evaluation with CheckM2/CheckM confirmed 60 bins with mean completeness 25.01% and contamination 2.98% (CheckM v1: 21.23% / 3.40%).","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:02:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5812016757","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWmxiIw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Correction: the baseline rerun (`baseline_rerun_autorestart1`) produced **60 bins**, not 25. The earlier reference to '25 bins' in comment 5810737932 reflected an intermediate count; the final evaluation with CheckM2/CheckM confirmed 60 bins with mean completeness 25.01% and contamination 2.98% (CheckM v1: 21.23% / 3.40% via py3.10 + LD_LIBRARY_PATH workaround).\n","createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:02:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5812019747","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":2,"title":"Can you try to create a small benchmark dataset for comebin ?","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T10:02:55Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2"}


